Luhmann called sociology "Die Abklärung der Aufklärung" in his Sociological Enlightenment 1. He drew a distinction between the individual-focused enlightenment and the sociological mission of focusing on an individual's contextual dependencies. In the same way, my improbable path to Sweden was shaped by all the amazing people around me. I deeply thank all of you from the bottom of my heart.

First, I thank my supervisors and mentors Károly Takács and Philipp Lorenz-Spreen for the kind guidance, all the inspiring meetings and, most importantly, the priceless support on my academic journey.

I especially want to thank all the dear and fantastic friends I made in Norrköping. I will miss all the fun evenings, the hours we spent in the library and most importantly all of you. You helped me grow tremendously, and I am deeply thankful for that.

I also want to thank the research group at SynoSys for integrating me so effortlessly. The dinner situations and coffee talks shaped the way I think about methods and science significantly. It is hard to imagine a better place to write this thesis.

Although this is my master's thesis, I want to extend my deep thanks to Elmar Schlüter for the outstanding support I received during my bachelor's. You are a fantastic researcher and a great role model for me. Whenever I learn something new now, I realize that you laid the foundation for it years ago. I also want to thank all my dear friends in Gießen for the coffee chats in the library, lunches and dinners. It was a wonderful time. 

Zuletzt und am Allerwichtigsten:\ Danke Mama und danke Papa! Ihr seid die besten Eltern, die ich mir jemals hätte wünschen können. Ich habe euch sehr lieb.

